+### Candidate r2: explicit finalizer decisions and failure-only output
+
+Classified assembly requires a top-level `status` or `decision` whose exact string is `accept` or `corrected`. At least one is required; when both are present they must be identical accepting strings. Reject/hold/missing, wrong types and conflicting values block assembly even if reasons or unrelated fields contain accepting words. Matching classification_context is a separate mandatory check.
