+Validate every entry's invariants, actual gate and required finalizer before exposing success output. Reserve only a new invocation directory and stage bytes in a private new sibling. Fsync all files/directories, atomically replace the empty reserve, and fsync the parent. An ordinary write/fsync/validation failure rolls back only tracked newly created inode-owned files/directories and retains at most a bounded failure.json in that invocation; no candidate, assembly, completed context or partial metrics may remain from the failed operation. Existing output/history is never adopted or cleaned. Persistent filesystem failure can also prevent durable failure diagnostics; it never authorizes success. Never consume hidden pending directories as evidence. Direct rejected gates retain failure-only diagnostics with their actual nonzero gate exit.
